// `--no-heap` proves the PROGRAM, and a program is what its entry points reach (KR-47). Importing a stdlib
// module whose error paths allocate is not reaching them: `Uuid`'s `Deserializable` boxes an error, its
// `format` interpolates, and none of that runs here. Until KR-47 the flag rejected every direct allocation
// in every emitted body, so this import alone was refused four times at stdlib lines the author never wrote.
//
// ⚠️ The import is the test and must not be tidied away as unused. The json and hex siblings are
// tests/noheap_flag_import_json.d and tests/noheap_flag_import_hex.d.
import { std::uuid::Uuid };
fn int32 main() { return 42; }
